### Sheet JSON (`cinakey.sheet/1.0`)
Stored on `entities.sheetFileId`. Fields: `schema`, `entityKind`, `version`, `parentFileId?`; character/creature: `look`, `age`, `build`, `wardrobe`, `personality`, `voiceNotes`, `identitySlots`, `expressionSlots[]`, `referenceSheetAssetId?`; location/prop: `notes`, `heroAssetIds[]`; style: `artStyleBlock?` (project ART STYLE paragraph), `palette`, `lighting`, `lensLook`, `filmGrain`, `mood`, `moodReferenceAssetIds[]`; all kinds: `draftPrompt?` (ad-hoc Generate panel).

### Prompt templates (asset + script text-first; blockout structured until 11C)
Zod schemas + deterministic renderers, parsers, and section validators in `@cinakey/shared` (`packages/shared/src/prompt-templates`). For **asset** and **script** sheets, the tip `promptSheets` **rendered prompt text is the source of truth**; `parseScriptPromptText` / `validateScriptPromptText` recover SHOTS and refs; structured JSON is derived on save for generation/blockout bridges. Blockout sheets still use structured JSON as source of truth (built on Update from the script). Project `artStyleBlock` (style entity) is kept consistent in ART STYLE sections; `projects.styleReferenceAssetId` is attached as a reference image on every GPT Image 2 job. Changing the style reference or ART STYLE marks dependent asset sheets `out_of_date`. Templates: character / creature / environment / product (GPT Image 2); script prompt per Part/sequence (Seedance 2.5); blockout sheet per Part. Example golden files live in `packages/shared/prompt-templates/examples/`.

## 7. Model adapters
Each model is one adapter declaring a capability manifest: id, kind (video/image/llm), operations (text-to-image, image-edit, text-to-video, image-to-video, upscale, extend, chat), inputs (text, startFrame, endFrame, referenceImages, audio), durations, **maxDurationSec** / **maxReferenceImages** (sequence splitting; Seedance 2.5: 30s / 30 refs), resolutions, aspect ratios, features (cameraControl, upscale, extend, inpaint...), and cost model. The UI shows only controls the manifest supports. Adapters implement: capabilities, estimateCost, buildRequest (shot + entities + style -> provider payload), submit, poll or webhook handling (optional verifyWebhook), collect outputs, optional isTransientError. Types live in `@cinakey/shared`. Launch adapters: seedance-2.5, gpt-image-2, deepseek. DeepSeek also exposes `streamChat` / `completeChat` helpers used by the copilot (token streaming into `copilotMessages`); the generation job runner still uses sync submit. `USE_MOCK_ADAPTERS=true` swaps provider HTTP for delayed sample outputs (same adapter ids), including a mock script proposal path for the copilot. Placeholder rates: gpt-image-2 10 credits/image; seedance-2.5 2 credits/second; deepseek 1 credit/1k tokens.

## 8. Blockout JSON format
Schema id `cinakey.blockout/2.0` (part-scoped). Types, validation, migrate `1.0`→`2.0`, sheet bridge, and pure engine (`camAt` / `objAt` / presets / retime) live in `packages/shared/src/blockout/`. Readers accept every id in `BLOCKOUT_READABLE_SCHEMAS`; older `1.0` docs migrate on read. Authority is the part document on `sequences.blockoutFileId` (versioned via `parentFileId`); per-shot `shots.blockoutFileId` is legacy read-only after migration.

- Document: `schema`, `version`, `parentFileId?`, `project` { `id`, `title`, `aspectRatio`, `fps` }, `sequenceId?`, `name`, `fps`, `frames`, `aspect`, `camera` { `sensor`, `keys[]` }, `objects[]`, `env?`, `shots[]` (cut markers), `guides?` per cut.
- Camera key: `id`, `f` (frame), `pos`, `target`, `focal`, `roll`, `ease` (`linear`|`in`|`out`|`inOut`|`hold`). Position/target: Catmull-Rom; focal/roll: linear; **hold = hard cut** (no tangent borrow).
- Object: `id`, `type` (character|creature|box|chair|table|door|car|wall|column|tree|sphere|fire|strip|mark|hare|raptor|light), `name`, `color`, `size`, `pos` [x,z], `y?`, `rot`, `keys[]`, optional `entityId` / `lightRole`.
- Object key: `f`, `x`, `z`, `y?`, `rot`, `ease` — linear position, shortest-path rotation.
- Cut marker: `n`, `start`, `end`, `desc`, optional `shotType`, `shotId`, `sceneHeading`, `lensMm`, `cameraMove`.
- **Blockout sheet bridge:** structured blockout prompt sheet maps onto one part document via `blockoutSheetToPartDocument`; selective rebuild keeps keys for cuts whose `scriptLineKey` is unchanged.

### Timeline JSON (`cinakey.timeline/1.0`)
Types and Zod validation live in `packages/shared/src/timeline.ts`. Stored on `timelineVersions.timelineFileId`.

- Document: `schema`, `version`, `parentFileId?`, `project` { `id`, `aspectRatio`, `fps` }, `durationSec`, `tracks[]`, `markers?[]`.
- Track: `id`, `kind` (`video`|`dialogue`|`music`|`sfx`|`titles`), `name`, `muted?`, `locked?`, `clips[]`.
- Clip: `id`, `startSec`, `durationSec`, `inSec`, `outSec`, `speed`, `source`, `volume?`, `fadeInSec?`, `fadeOutSec?`, `linkedShotId?`.
- Source: `take` { `takeId`, `shotId`, `assetId`, `proxyAssetId?` } | `asset` { `assetId` } | `text` { `text`, `styleId` (`lower-third`|`centered`|`caption`), `lines?` }.
- Export caps (MVP): long edge ≤ 1920, duration ≤ 300s (`TIMELINE_EXPORT_MAX_*` in shared). Playback prefers proxies for video and originals for audio.

## 9. Credits and jobs
Credits ledger is append-only (`grant` / `reserve` / `settle` / `refund`). Balance = latest `balanceAfter` for the workspace; mutations reject any write that would make balance negative. New workspaces receive a one-time **100-credit** starter grant (`workspaces.starterCreditsGrantedAt`). Flow: estimate cost from the adapter -> check optional `projects.spendCapCredits` (project net spend + estimate must not exceed cap) -> reserve credits -> action calls provider (`queued` → `submitted` → `running`) -> poll on a schedule (backoff) or receive webhook (HTTP action with `GENERATION_WEBHOOK_SECRET` signature check) -> save outputs as assets (lineage: job, model, prompt, seed, input asset ids); video jobs with `shotId` create a take; video jobs with `sequenceId` and no `shotId` create a master asset + per-shot trimmed takes; image jobs with `shotId` set `shots.keyframeAssetId` -> settle (`delta = estimated − actual`, actual ≤ estimated) or refund the full reserve on final failure (`refunded`). UI confirms runs whose estimate exceeds `COST_CONFIRM_THRESHOLD_CREDITS` (50). Automatic retry on transient provider errors (max 3 submit attempts). Rate limits (per user / hour): generation starts 20, copilot turns 60, project creates 10, export records 30, staff grants 60. Dev-only `grantDev` requires staff or `ALLOW_DEV_CREDITS=true`. Staff grants/refunds require a reason and write `auditLog`.

## 10. Roadmap
Phase 1 MVP (solo creators): modules above marked [MVP], including Phase 10 launch essentials. Gate: 50 creators finish a video end to end; median idea-to-export under 3 hours; 40% start a second project.
Phase 2 Pro and collaboration: project members, share links, admin platform with RBAC, animatic, lip sync and AI voice, batch generation, branching, aspect-ratio variants, OTIO/XML export, more templates, video to R2 when egress justifies it (egressEvents inform the decision).
Phase 3 Teams: workspace roles, shot assignment, client review and approval, real-time co-editing, brand kits, SSO, usage reports.
Phase 4 Platform: public API, pipeline templates, custom model and identity training, more models via adapters, marketplace.
Out of the MVP: own foundation model, models beyond Seedance 2.5 / GPT Image 2 / DeepSeek, frame interpolation and frame repair, members and sharing, full admin platform, server-side rendering, mobile editing, co-editing, C2PA-embedded MP4s.

## 11. Trust and safety
Prompt and output moderation hooks run before provider submit and after collect (in-code block/flag rules → `moderationFlags` queue for staff). Likeness-consent required on uploads that contain a real face and enforced on generation reference assets (`likenessConsent === false` rejects). **C2PA provenance on exported MP4s is deferred**: browser Mediabunny export cannot embed C2PA cleanly in MVP — document as TODO until a server-side or muxer path exists. Clear commercial-use terms; documented data handling for ByteDance, OpenAI and DeepSeek. Email via Resend (`RESEND_API_KEY`); users may disable email in Settings.

## 12. Code conventions
- **Monorepo folders:** `apps/web` (creator React + Vite app), `packages/backend` (Convex project), `packages/shared` (types used by web and backend), `packages/config` (shared tsconfig / ESLint / Prettier). Do not put web or Convex files at the repo root.
- **Web (`apps/web`):** `src/app` (routes, shell, protected route), `src/features/<module>` (one folder per product module), `src/components` (shared UI, including `ui/` for shadcn-style primitives), `src/lib` (utilities). Path alias `@/` → `apps/web/src/`.
- **Backend (`packages/backend`):** `convex/` (schema, auth, functions), `convex/adapters` (model adapters), `convex/storage.ts` (sole storage module — the only code that may call `ctx.storage.*`). Generated `api` / data model types are exported from `@cinakey/backend` for apps to import.
- **Shared (`packages/shared`):** Cross-cutting types and schemas (e.g. model capability types, `cinakey.blockout/2.0` + pure engine in `src/blockout/`, **`cinakey.timeline/1.0`** in `timeline.ts`, **prompt-template Zod schemas/renderers** in `src/prompt-templates/`). Import as `@cinakey/shared` — no deep relative imports across packages.
- **Adding a new app or package:** create `apps/<name>` or `packages/<name>` with its own `package.json` (scoped `@cinakey/...`), extend `@cinakey/config` for TS/ESLint/Prettier, add workspace deps with `"*"`, and ensure root Turborepo tasks (`dev`, `build`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`) pick it up via workspaces.
- **Naming:** React components and files that export them use PascalCase (`ProjectsPage.tsx`). Functions, hooks, and variables use camelCase. Convex modules use camelCase filenames matching their export surface (`users.ts`, `auth.ts`). Adapter ids use kebab-case (`seedance-2.5`). CSS prefers Tailwind utilities; shared class merging via `cn()` in `apps/web/src/lib/utils.ts`.
- **UI kit:** Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui-style Radix primitives. Dark-first zinc/neutral studio theme (IBM Plex Sans). App shell: left nav + top bar with user menu. Prefer composition over cards for chrome; cards only when they contain an interaction.
- **Imports:** Web imports Convex `api` from `@cinakey/backend` and shared types from `@cinakey/shared`. Prefer named exports for components.
- **Testing:** Vitest + Testing Library + jsdom (web). Colocate `*.test.ts(x)` next to the code under test. Run from root with `npm run test` (Turborepo) or per package. Lint with ESLint; format with Prettier; typecheck with `npm run typecheck` (strict TypeScript).
- **Backend rules:** Provider secrets only via Convex env (`npx convex env set` from `packages/backend`). Never call Convex file storage outside `packages/backend/convex/storage.ts`. AI model HTTP only through adapters.

